<subpara id="RM0000013JZ00JX_03" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000013JZ00JX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000013JZ00JX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000047W00000">
<scantool type="4"/>
<testtitle>Read TaSCAN Data (A/T Hydraulic Pressure (CVT Hydraulic Pressure))</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), display the [ECU Data Monitor] screen according to the screen display, and check the computer data.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>[Diagnosis menu screen: Powertrain → TCCS → ECU Data Monitor]</title>
<tgroup cols="4">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.54in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="1.48in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
<ptxt>[Symbol]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item Description</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Reference Value</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A/T Hydraulic Pressure</ptxt>
<ptxt>[THO]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Indicates CVT hydraulic pressure</ptxt>
<ptxt>Display range: -0.625 to 9.576MPa</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>During belt clamping pressure inspection (at stall)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4.22 to 5.12MPa</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.07in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>NG</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>OK</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000013JZ00JX_04_0003" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM0000013JZ00JX_04_0004" fin="false">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000013JZ00JX_04_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___000047Y00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Oil Pressure Sensor - Engine Control Computer)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the wire harness and connector inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/>.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the oil pressure sensor connector and connector A of the engine control computer.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals of the engine control computer and the oil pressure sensor vehicle side connector. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000000FSD00RX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C125748J03" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Name)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A70(VCPT) - 3(VC)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A71(PTO) - 2(PTO)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A94(EPTO) - 1(E2)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A70 (VCPT) and 3 (VC) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A71 (PTO) and 2 (PTO) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A94 (EPTO) and 1 (E2) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000013JZ00JX_04_0002" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000013JZ00JX_04_0008" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000013JZ00JX_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___000047X00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Engine Control Computer (VCPT Power Source)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect connector A of the engine control computer.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the terminals of the oil pressure sensor vehicle side connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C125747J05" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC1" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Name)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
